runs to completion (rc=0) but stdout does not match .expected. Not further diagnosed. UPDATE 2026-08-30 (seat01): root mechanism now precisely characterized, not fixed -- a mixed int/real comparison's success value is never numeric-promoted (Icon: `6.2 ~= 4` returns `4.0`; SCRIP returns `4`). Same root cause as ck.icn's own "loses its real-ness" note. Confirmed via the emitted .s: the codegen copies operand b's pre-call descriptor verbatim on success, and rt_jct_relop only returns a boolean, carrying no promoted value at all -- the same bare-copy shape exists in by_name_dispatch.c's generic relop dispatch too (2 call sites found, possibly more not searched for). See FINDING-2026-08-30-seat01-icon-relop-success-value-never-numeric-promoted.md. Also noted there: an unrelated, unexplained oddity where a real LITERAL directly in a relop (not through a variable) fails outright instead of just returning the wrong type.
